<p>Israeli strikes continued across Lebanon over the weekend in the latest development in the Israel–Hezbollah conflict, with reported fatalities nearing 400 as attacks expanded to include targets in and around Beirut as well as southern areas. Israel’s military said it targeted Iranian commanders in Beirut and described the operation as an effort to stop Iranian “terrorist elements” from establishing themselves in Lebanese territory. The fighting has also included ground clashes. France 24 reported that two Israeli soldiers were killed overnight in fighting with Hezbollah in southern Lebanon, and another report described clashes in eastern Lebanon as strikes hit Beirut’s southern suburbs. The rising toll and widening geography underscore the risk that the violence could spread further in a densely populated region.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MtdpU0PPQDy21Zd6XkSYEytN0CxbWlTQo5XWTEdf4vS6UANBVG3Toyv_wVRYx3DBL041aX0NBTuaCJ6J7GASwbpd5KQOKitLEHkTGxhUSBMN-Gqtw_QIfVSIyzkdzmaOo7fendt2pJZeahG7MA9tx3gkx-O4NGGbCEdWJaqvu8lxOk0Sxy-YjtRWV44_dB-fFj9gY2kj4YOoon0CoQ' alt='' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Central Beirut hit: France 24 reported an Israeli strike on a hotel in central Beirut, suggesting strikes have reached beyond the south and Beirut’s southern suburbs.</li><li>Southern deaths: Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon on Sunday killed at least 20 people, according to reports.</li><li>Wider regional backdrop: Euronews said Tehran continued missile and drone attacks across the Gulf as Israel expanded operations in southern Lebanon.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israel Defense Forces: The military said it would &quot;not allow Iranian terrorist elements to establish themselves in Lebanese territory&quot; and described strikes as aimed at that objective. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/many-people-dead-as-israeli-strikes-continue-in-lebanon/article70719828.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www